riscos-risc3d (0.8-1) rol; urgency=medium

  * rol-3d 0.8: arrays and indices from a program's memory are given to
    Linux's Mesa as memory (it streams them into one buffer of its own),
    not each put in a fresh buffer object; OP_UPLOADS chooses (for
    comparing). The modules are unchanged (RISC3D 0.03, Linux3D 0.02).

 -- Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0000

riscos-risc3d (0.7-1) rol; urgency=medium

  * rol-3d 0.7, RISC3D module 0.03, Linux3D 0.02: RISC3D_Info says when
    Linux's Mesa draws in software (no GPU driver), so that riscos-mesa
    can keep its own faster software renderer there. *RISC3D says it too.

