riscos-risc3d (0.6-1) rol; urgency=medium

  * RISC3D 0.6: GL_EXT_direct_state_access (objects, matrices and arrays
    by name), the last of the extensions riscos-mesa offers. rol-3d says
    which commands it takes, so a newer library offers only what it has.

 -- Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

riscos-risc3d (0.5-1) rol; urgency=medium

  * RISC3D 0.5: OpenGL 3.0/3.1 and OpenGL ES 3.0/3.1 (uniform blocks,
    transform feedback, sync objects, instanced arrays, integer
    attributes, sampler objects, indirect draws, compute shaders), and
    the rest of the extensions riscos-mesa offers in OpenGL 2.1. Where
    the driver's compatibility profile stops at 2.1 (Mesa's v3d), a
    program that asks for OpenGL 3.1 gets 3.1 without it.

 -- Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000

riscos-risc3d (0.4-1) rol; urgency=medium

  * RISC3D 0.4: OpenGL ES 1.1 (on desktop OpenGL: Debian's Mesa has no
    GLES 1), and the extensions riscos-mesa offers in OpenGL ES 2 (base
    vertex and instanced draws, vertex array objects, mapped ranges,
    separate programs, debug output, 3D textures and others).

